note bay 3 review of 2d6ed949: symlnk on a well-formed two-record packet of 4097 bytes, one past the 4096-byte
note cap that symlnk keeps under omc 564c5835, traps 3 before any kernel call (OMEGESE s10); ngrun refuses
note symlnk (121) only after that check, and the exec argument cap must not reach it.
fn main to int
a = new uchar 4097 120
put a 0 2
put a 1 0
put a 2 248
put a 3 15
put a 4092 3
put a 4093 0
put a 4094 97
put a 4095 98
put a 4096 99
k = symlnk a 0 4097
ret int and k 255
end
